    "summary": "FFmpeg's RASC video decoder (decode_dlta in libavcodec/rasc.c) performs 32-bit reads and writes...",
    "details": "FFmpeg's RASC video decoder (`decode_dlta` in `libavcodec/rasc.c`) performs 32-bit reads and writes at the row cursor before the `NEXT_LINE` row-boundary check and validates the DLTA region in pixel rather than byte units, so a DLTA run on a PAL8 frame can access several bytes past the row allocation. A crafted media stream using the RASC FourCC, decoded by libavcodec, triggers a bitstream-controlled out-of-bounds heap write and adjacent out-of-bounds read, leading to memory corruption.",
    "severity": [
        {
            "type": "CVSS_V3",
            "score": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:H",
